    "result_text": "Jobs can now be marked billable or non-billable, and each job's page shows which it is. `bin/e2e` builds and the acceptance test passes. That test only checks what the page shows for a job seeded as non-billable. Nothing has exercised the toggle button or the new update endpoint yet.\n\nNote: your request mentioned an OfficeFloor server, but this app is Spring Boot (as `CLAUDE.md` says), so the server changes follow Spring conventions.\n\n**Database**\n- `V50__project_billable.sql` adds a `billable` column to `project`. Existing jobs default to billable.\n\n**Server**\n- **`Project` / `ProjectResponse`:** jobs have a `billable` flag, and the API returns it.\n- **New endpoint:** `PUT /api/projects/{id}/billable` with `{ \"billable\": true|false }`. A change writes `PROJECT_BILLABLE_SET id=\u2026 billable=\u2026` to the audit log, like the existing budget and status changes.\n- **`ProjectRequest`:** takes an optional `billable` when a job is created, defaulting to billable. The create form in the UI doesn't offer it yet, so new jobs from the UI start billable.\n- **Test seeding:** `TestSupportController` reads `billable` for projects and treats them as billable unless the fixture says `false`.\n\n**Front end**\n- The job page shows `Billable` or `Non-billable` (`data-testid=\"project-billable\"`).\n- Next to it is a button (`project-billable-toggle`) that switches the setting and updates the page in place.\n- If saving fails, an error message appears (`project-billable-error`).\n\nNo existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.",
